  "question": {
    "text": "A long straight wire of radius ' $a$ ' caries a steady current $\\mathrm{i}$. The current is uniformly distributed across its cross section. The ratio of the magnetic field at $\\frac{a}{2}$ and $2 a$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "lBWkJ",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{4}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2so8r",
      "text": "\n$4$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "YE4lo",
      "text": "\n$1$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "DZFDZ",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{B} 2 \\pi \\frac{\\mathrm{a}}{2}=\\mu_0 \\frac{\\mathrm{i}}{\\pi \\mathrm{a}^2}\\left(\\frac{\\pi \\mathrm{a}^2}{4}\\right)$\n$\\mathrm{B}_1=\\frac{\\mu_0 \\mathrm{i}}{4 \\pi \\mathrm{a}} \\quad \\ldots$ (i)\n$\\mathrm{B}_2 2 \\pi(2 \\mathrm{a})=\\mu_0 \\mathrm{i}$\n$\\mathrm{B}_2=\\frac{\\mu_0 \\mathrm{i}}{4 \\pi \\mathrm{a}} \\quad \\dots (ii)$\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{B}_1}{\\mathrm{~B}_2}=1$",
